title: Support OpenAI-compatible Responses API where available
updated_at: "2026-08-02T06:12:48Z"
---
Many OpenAI-compatible providers now offer the Responses API (/v1/responses) alongside or instead of Chat Completions. When available, the Responses API offers better statefulness, tool use, and reasoning content handling.\n\nResearch which upstream providers support it and add routing logic to prefer Responses API when available, falling back to Chat Completions.\n\nProviders to investigate: OpenAI, OpenAI-Codex, local proxies, and any custom upstream that advertises /v1/responses.
## Requirements (updated)

- Custom providers should have a config flag `use_responses_api` (default: true) to enable the Responses API path.
- When enabled but the provider returns 404 or otherwise indicates the Responses API is not available, log a warning and automatically fall back to the Chat Completions API for subsequent requests.
- Detection should be automatic: try Responses API first (when enabled), cache the result (available/not-available) per provider, and avoid repeated failed attempts.
